---
layout: base.njk
---
{#- The newest entry wears no band (2026-11-04): the masthead stands in for
    it, daily or essay. It stays tonight's sky, not that post's — nothing
    here claims they're the same. Every entry after keeps its band. -#}
{#- The page's one h1 (2026-11-11): the site name is a wordmark image link in
    the header, so a heading for it is read aloud only. -#}
<h1 class="sr-only">{{ site.title }}</h1>
{#- The rail (2026-11-13, after maggieappleton.com's TOC): the stream's
    entries down the left gutter, each day's date big and its subjects under
    it, sticky, the one you're in lit. Wide screens only (CSS, "the rail");
    the ids it links to are the li's and linkSubjects' date-prefixed ones. -#}
<nav class="rail" aria-label="On this page"><div class="rail-inner">
  {#- A row is a label and a tick. At rest only the ticks show, a thin strip
      against the shell's left edge; hover or focus opens the labels (CSS,
      "the rail"). Rows group by day: an essay on a day that also has a daily
      joins that day's group, so a group opens on a new date only. -#}
  {% set five = collections.stream | limit(5) %}
  {% for entry in five %}
  {% set item = entry.essay or entry.post %}
  {% set d = item.date | dateSlug %}
  {% set prev = five[loop.index0 - 1] if not loop.first %}
  {% set newDay = loop.first or ((prev.essay or prev.post).date | dateSlug) != d %}
  {% if newDay %}{% if not loop.first %}</div>{% endif %}
  <div class="rail-day">
    <a class="rail-row rail-row-day" href="#{{ ('essay-' + d) if entry.kind == "essay" else d }}"><span class="rail-label">{{ item.date | shortDate }}</span><span class="rail-tick"></span></a>
  {% endif %}
  {% if entry.kind == "essay" %}
    <a class="rail-row rail-row-essay" href="#essay-{{ d }}"><span class="rail-label"><span class="rail-kind">deep thoughts</span>{{ item.title }}</span><span class="rail-tick"></span></a>
  {% else %}
    {% for s in item.content | dayContents(d + "-") %}<a class="rail-row" href="#{{ s.id }}"><span class="rail-label">{{ s.title }}</span><span class="rail-tick"></span></a>{% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if loop.last %}</div>{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</div></nav>
{% include "rail-script.njk" %}
<ul class="post-list">
  {% for entry in collections.stream | limit(5) %}
  {% if entry.kind == "essay" %}
  {#- An essay in the stream is its lede and a link, never the text: the
      full piece has one home. The kicker marks it as the other kind of post,
      since a titled daily wears the same head. -#}
  {% set e = entry.essay %}
  <li class="stream-essay" id="essay-{{ e.date | dateSlug }}">
    <div class="entry-head"{% if not loop.first %} style="--day-sky:url({{ e.date | daySky }})"{% endif %}>
      <span class="entry-kind">deep thoughts</span>
      <a class="post-list-title" href="{{ e.url }}">{{ e.title }}</a>
      <p class="post-list-subdate">{{ e.date | readableDate }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="post-body"><p>{{ e.blurb }}</p></div>
    <a class="more" href="{{ e.url }}">read the rest →</a>
  </li>
  {% else %}
  {% set post = entry.post %}
  {#- Whole days since 2026-11-13: homeBody's 1500-character cut and its
      "read the rest" link are gone (why: eleventy.config.js, above the
      limit filter). -#}
  {% set d = post.date | dateSlug %}
  <li id="{{ d }}">
    <div class="entry-head"{% if not loop.first %} style="--day-sky:url({{ post.date | daySky }})"{% endif %}>
      {% if post.data.title %}
      <a class="post-list-title" href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
      <p class="post-list-subdate">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</p>
      {% else %}
      <a class="post-list-date" href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</a>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="post-body">{{ post.content | spoilers | linkSubjects(true, d + "-") | safe }}</div>
  </li>
  {% endif %}
  {% else %}
  <li class="empty">Nothing here yet.</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

{% if collections.stream | length > 5 %}
<p class="all-link"><a href="/archive/">all posts →</a></p>
{% endif %}
